ield/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f29572bc-a376-5e26-908c-dd4693b8b94a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284813} :answer-field/id #uuid "36b1c7be-4271-51b0-b452-145e670ba402" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284812}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "298f431b-16f6-54d9-a1a9-ec74c0465162" :question/math-academy-id "q-138783" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995865/assets/c1d9f53c6aed4acd378f8554df5c8beaaea81e169b5284e51f87204a87b3d53d.png)\n\nA housing complex designed by an architect is shown in the coordinate plane as the region $R$ with vertices $ABCD.$ A highway lies on the line $l$ with equation $2x+y+1=0.$ The area of the complex is $16$ hectares.\n\nCurrent part:\n\n$$\nX+Y=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,Z=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices above. Knowing that the matrix representation $T=[\\begin{aligned}{t}_{11} & {t}_{12} \\\\ {t}_{21} & {t}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$ of a linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=XZ+YZ,\n$$\n\nfind the values ${t}_{ij}.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{11}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{12}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{21}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{22}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nXZ+YZ=(X+Y)Z.\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =XZ+YZ \\\\  & =(X+Y)Z \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284814 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c9849b9-397b-5fb9-bb4b-01f3d013c5c2" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Polygon Under the Action of a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "883e7a0b-d26a-59b0-aad2-6e760c3207b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284816}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "883e7a0b-d26a-59b0-aad2-6e760c3207b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284816} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e3fbd50-cc65-5ad3-bea8-113338daa622" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284815} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf221ee4-f7b4-5fb1-9803-ea36e2649e69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284818}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf221ee4-f7b4-5fb1-9803-ea36e2649e69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284818} :answer-field/id #uuid "44266677-451a-5fe2-bb5e-cbb7add78b27" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284817} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f8f0deaf-3a47-5922-9edd-0c6e2a12f201" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8f0deaf-3a47-5922-9edd-0c6e2a12f201" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284820} :answer-field/id #uuid "33e2f335-2675-5490-929a-525e41e7ae7a" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284819} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d8f4a61-6240-5aac-94e8-814383d4cceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284822}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d8f4a61-6240-5aac-94e8-814383d4cceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284822} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fb9d0ac-b069-5590-9b79-3ab3faea198b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284821}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c89b287d-33ff-50df-954b-524d0b0a1926" :question/math-academy-id "q-138784" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995865/assets/c1d9f53c6aed4acd378f8554df5c8beaaea81e169b5284e51f87204a87b3d53d.png)\n\nA housing complex designed by an architect is shown in the coordinate plane as the region $R$ with vertices $ABCD.$ A highway lies on the line $l$ with equation $2x+y+1=0.$ The area of the complex is $16$ hectares.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n$$\nX+Y=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,Z=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices above. Knowing that the matrix representation $T=[\\begin{aligned}{t}_{11} & {t}_{12} \\\\ {t}_{21} & {t}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$ of a linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=XZ+YZ,\n$$\n\nfind the values ${t}_{ij}.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{11}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{12}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{21}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{22}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-1$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nThe architect is expanding the plan of the housing complex. The transformation $T$ from part 1 maps the current plan of the housing complex $ABCD$ to the new plan ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}{D}^{′}.$ Find the vertices of the new housing complex.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${A}^{′}(-9,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n${B}^{′}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,14)$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${C}^{′}(-21,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n${D}^{′}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-4}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,0)$" :question/worked-solution "In part 1, we found that the matrix representation of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of the field under the action of $T,$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $ABCD:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 7 & 7 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 7 & 7 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-9 & -21 & -21 & -9 \\\\ 4 & 14 & 10 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}{D}^{′}$ are $(-9,4),$ $(-21,14),$ $(-21,10),$ and $(-9,0),$ as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995865/assets/7430fd0c1e3a4c94e951eb1cf133e5c155f7a7b605a46b4b2272bf30fbb688e2.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284823 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dae3b81-42bf-5d8f-a573-f4e8f864bcf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dae3b81-42bf-5d8f-a573-f4e8f864bcf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284825} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f12e676-d778-55a6-bc23-f52756889a29" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284824}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6bb7d03d-675a-5ff1-80f4-70e2c7657223" :question/math-academy-id "q-138785" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995865/assets/c1d9f53c6aed4acd378f8554df5c8beaaea81e169b5284e51f87204a87b3d53d.png)\n\nA housing complex designed by an architect is shown in the coordinate plane as the region $R$ with vertices $ABCD.$ A highway lies on the line $l$ with equation $2x+y+1=0.$ The area of the complex is $16$ hectares.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n$$\nX+Y=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,Z=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices above. Knowing that the matrix representation $T=[\\begin{aligned}{t}_{11} & {t}_{12} \\\\ {t}_{21} & {t}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$ of a linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=XZ+YZ,\n$$\n\nfind the values ${t}_{ij}.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{11}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{12}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{21}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{22}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-1$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nThe architect is expanding the plan of the housing complex. The transformation $T$ from part 1 maps the current plan of the housing complex $ABCD$ to the new plan ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}{D}^{′}.$ Find the vertices of the new housing complex.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${A}^{′}(-9,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n${B}^{′}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-21$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,14)$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${C}^{′}(-21,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $10$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n${D}^{′}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-9$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,0)$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nThe area of the new housing complex is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \nhectares." :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $R$ (the old housing complex) and the area of the image $T(R)$ (the new housing complex) under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(R))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(R)\n$$\n\nWe're given that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(R)=16\\,\\text{hectares}.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of the matrix $T$ (found in part 1), we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot (-1)-(2)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(R)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(R) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 16 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the new housing complex is $48$ hectares."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284826 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0cbb889-0fe1-5347-94a3-53db3ff9a95c" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertices of a Polygon Given Its Image Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2373e93f-3a70-5dc9-8f11-0d3001ec0b62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2373e93f-3a70-5dc9-8f11-0d3001ec0b62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284828} :answer-field/id #uuid "81f84f96-477c-5c7b-ab0d-eb1f36f66952" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284827} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f52b1deb-f129-59d5-8afa-fa9c9e8e07a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f52b1deb-f129-59d5-8afa-fa9c9e8e07a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284830} :answer-field/id #uuid "c145a8a5-8c71-56c7-8cda-0e54100f3b56" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284829} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c04263c7-bdbf-5bf7-9210-d472b0daebd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c04263c7-bdbf-5bf7-9210-d472b0daebd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284832} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa3dcd00-81a3-5119-83a2-1ed13ab6f393" :answe