                             \n$\\,{t}_{12}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{21}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{22}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-1$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nThe architect is expanding the plan of the housing complex. The transformation $T$ from part 1 maps the current plan of the housing complex $ABCD$ to the new plan ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}{D}^{′}.$ Find the vertices of the new housing complex.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${A}^{′}(-9,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n${B}^{′}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-21$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,14)$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${C}^{′}(-21,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $10$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n${D}^{′}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-9$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,0)$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nThe area of the new housing complex is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $48$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \nhectares.\n\nCurrent part:\n\nA triangular recreational area next to the housing complex is mapped to a larger recreational area under the action of $T.$ The larger recreational area has vertices ${L}^{′}(-15,4),$ ${M}^{′}(-15,2),$ and ${N}^{′}(-21,6).$ Find the corresponding vertices of the smaller recreational area.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $L(5,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n$M($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,8)$\n$\\,$\n$N(7,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$" :question/worked-solution "In part 1, we found that the matrix representation of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we create a matrix $Y$ containing all of the vertices of the larger recreational area:\n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}-15 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, if $X$ denotes the matrix that contains the corresponding vertices of the smaller recreational area, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot X & =Y \\\\ T\\cdot X & =[\\begin{aligned}-15 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-15 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-15 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inverse of $T$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-1)(-3)-0}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-15 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-15 & -15 & -21 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}15 & 15 & 21 \\\\ 18 & 24 & 24\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertices of the smaller recreational area are $L(5,6),$ $M(5,8),$ and $N(7,8).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284833 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15e8730b-c59a-5897-8c83-073b54f517a9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Given by an Equation in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b732e67-b272-5e0a-8135-7852163fc087" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284835}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b732e67-b272-5e0a-8135-7852163fc087" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284835} :answer-field/id #uuid "ceaa648a-b074-51bc-bfb4-ab5cdff84d97" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284834} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29c3f4c8-0685-5108-986f-da507127ad10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284837}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29c3f4c8-0685-5108-986f-da507127ad10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284837} :answer-field/id #uuid "da63ed26-2492-5299-83d6-3c95f9cd36d7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284836}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a8d5ec0c-5b65-5d4b-8a35-8688ea93cb0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-138787" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13995865/assets/c1d9f53c6aed4acd378f8554df5c8beaaea81e169b5284e51f87204a87b3d53d.png)\n\nA housing complex designed by an architect is shown in the coordinate plane as the region $R$ with vertices $ABCD.$ A highway lies on the line $l$ with equation $2x+y+1=0.$ The area of the complex is $16$ hectares.\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\n$$\nX+Y=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,Z=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices above. Knowing that the matrix representation $T=[\\begin{aligned}{t}_{11} & {t}_{12} \\\\ {t}_{21} & {t}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$ of a linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=XZ+YZ,\n$$\n\nfind the values ${t}_{ij}.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{11}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-3$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{12}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $0$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{21}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{22}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-1$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nThe architect is expanding the plan of the housing complex. The transformation $T$ from part 1 maps the current plan of the housing complex $ABCD$ to the new plan ${A}^{′}{B}^{′}{C}^{′}{D}^{′}.$ Find the vertices of the new housing complex.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${A}^{′}(-9,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n${B}^{′}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-21$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,14)$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${C}^{′}(-21,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $10$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n${D}^{′}($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $-9$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,0)$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nThe area of the new housing complex is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $48$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \nhectares.\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nA triangular recreational area next to the housing complex is mapped to a larger recreational area under the action of $T.$ The larger recreational area has vertices ${L}^{′}(-15,4),$ ${M}^{′}(-15,2),$ and ${N}^{′}(-21,6).$ Find the corresponding vertices of the smaller recreational area.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $L(5,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $6$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n$\\,$\n$M($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $5$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$,8)$\n$\\,$\n$N(7,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $8$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nThe architect finds the image of the line $l$ under the action of $T$ and places another highway on the plan from this image. The equation of the line on which the new highway lies, in **standard form**, is\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$x\\,+\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$y\\,=\\,3.$" :question/worked-solution "In part 1, we found that the matrix representation of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that the line $2x+y+1=0$ passes through the points $U(-1,1)$ and $V(0,-1)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $U$ and $V$ under the action of $T,$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${U}^{′}(3,-3)$ and ${V}^{′}(0,1).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${U}^{′}$ and ${V}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-3) & =\\frac{1-(-3)}{0-3}(x-3) \\\\ y+3 & =-\\frac{4}{3}(x-3) \\\\ 3y+9 & =-4x+12 \\\\ 4x+3y+9 & =12 \\\\ 4x+3y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284838 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba6081fd-7ac0-58e2-b2d7-ec659c2b6e2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba6081fd-7ac0-58e2-b2d7-ec659c2b6e2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284840} :answer-field/id #uuid "bccddd7d-1c52-572c-a2cc-102594d02482" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284839} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id 